From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:50:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] kosmickrisp: add a lazily allocated memory type with the
 fdm experiment

On its FDM path native Alyx creates its subsampled multisampled colour
target as a transient attachment and asks for DEVICE_LOCAL |
LAZILY_ALLOCATED memory. KosmicKrisp had no such type, the allocation
failed and the game bound VK_NULL_HANDLE, which crashed in
kk_BindImageMemory2.

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=fdm, add a DEVICE_LOCAL | LAZILY_ALLOCATED type
on the system heap. It is fully backed, so input attachment and custom
resolve reads of those images still work, and only images with
TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT usage may use it; buffers, imports and other images
exclude it.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

